-- Option+H: the BrailleCraft keys for VoiceOver.
on run
	my speak("BrailleCraft keys, each with the Option key. 7, the translated line. 8, the current style; twice quickly in a table, the row and column. 9, the location: page, line and column. 0, the document name, its tab, and status line. Comma, the position on the line; twice quickly, the characters to the end of the line. Period, the number of characters on the line; twice quickly, the left spaces. L, the last word on the line. Semicolon, the cursor to the translated line and back. T, the current table entry. C, whether a braille keyboard is connected. H, this list. The open documents are tabs of the window: Command+Shift+Right Bracket and Left Bracket, or Control+Tab and Control+Shift+Tab, move between them, and Control+Tab works with every keyboard layout; Command+W closes one; the Window menu has Move Tab to New Window and Merge All Windows. The keys work in a document window; elsewhere they say not in document window. In VoiceOver Utility, General, Allow VoiceOver to be controlled with AppleScript must be on for VoiceOver to speak them in its own voice.")
end run
